      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Here has additional information that in my case, I let my game use global settings and change global setting directly while testing, set Vsync to on doesn't cause issue for me but once I set Vsync option to \"fast\", it will 100% cause this issue and it's the only one that can cause issue for me ! (plus this video player error is also the major issue that cause two of vket main worlds get very terrible fps drop, fps boost from 15 to about 90 after do this workaround)\nMonitor refresh rate is 144 and I use launch option to make my game run at 144fps also.\nWin 10 21H1\nIntel 8700K\nRTX 3080 with driver version 471.68\nSet to anything other than \"fast\" for VRChat at program settings is my final solution.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
